{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNdEwU9tF5hnhRDWizJD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #357 as **done**: it goes to the triage engineer for planning, and the engineer worker will implement it. The routing file is at `.ard/357/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **What the issue asks:** when a push or token request fails with a temporary GitHub problem, such as a server error, a network failure or a failed token request, the committer should retry with increasing waits instead of failing the job. If the problem outlasts the retry budget, the job should end with a temporary cause so the Reaper retries it, rather than ending as failed.\n- **Why only the engineer:** the change stays inside `internal/gitx`, `internal/committer` and the job close-out path. The engineer is the only triage role besides lead, and `eng-review` runs on every pull request anyway, so no `review:` entry was needed.\n\nOpen issues I listed for maintainers:\n- **Extra case in the comments:** a comment reports a protected-branch rejection that looks like a race with another push. The plan has to decide whether it belongs in this change. If it does, a rejection that persists after a fresh fetch should end the job needing a human, not failed.\n- **Push that already landed:** a retry must compare the upstream branch with the pushed commit so it never writes a second commit.\n- **Close-out cause:** this changes how the Reaper sees the job, so the plan should confirm which existing temporary cause to reuse."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":11926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_u